{title: Battle Hymn Of The Republic}
{key: G}
{x_theme: praise, altar, grace-mercy}
{x_source: chrd:battle_hymn_of_the_republic.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
[G]Glory! Glory! Hallelujah!
[C]Glory! Glory! Halle[G]lujah!
Glory! Glory! Halle[G]lu - [Em]jah!
His [Am]truth is [G]mar - [D7]ching [G]on.

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]Mine eyes have seen the glory of the coming of the Lord;
He is [C]trampling out the vintage where the [G]grapes of wrath are stored.
He hath loosed the fateful lightning of His [G]terri[B7]ble swift [Em]sword;
His [Am]truth is [G]mar - [D7]ching [G]on.

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]I have seen Him in the watch-fires of a hundred circling camps;
They have [C]builded Him an altar in the evening [G]dews and damps.
I can read His righteous sentence by the [G]dim and [B7]flaring [Em]lamps;
His [Am]day is [G]mar - [D7]ching [G]on!

{comment: Verse 3}
[G]I have read a fiery gospel writ in burnished rows of steel;
"As ye [C]deal with my contemners, so with you my [G]grace shall deal;
Let the Hero, born of woman, crush the [G]serpent [B7]with his [Em]heel,
Since [Am]God is [G]mar - [D7]ching [G]on."

{comment: Verse 4}
[G]He has sounded forth the trumpet that shall never call retreat;
He is [C]sifting out the hearts of men be[G]fore His judgment-seat;
Oh, be swift, my soul, to answer Him! be [G]jubi - [B7]lant, my [Em]feet!
Our [Am]God is [G]mar - [D7]ching [G]on!

{comment: Verse 5}
[G]In the beauty of the lilies Christ was born across the sea,
With a [C]glory in his bosom that trans[G]figures you and me;
As he died to make men holy, let us [G]die to [B7]make men [Em]free,
While [Am]God is [G]mar - [D7]ching [G]on.
